S136 src=premise lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: If the traveler can reach island 71, then the traveler can reach island 72.
S137 src=cite kid=K001 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Mathematical induction: if a property P holds for the number 1, and whenever P holds for a positive integer n it also holds for n + 1, then P holds for every positive integer n.
S138 src=cite kid=K001 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: (Infinite descent may be used as induction combined with contradiction; no separate rule is needed.)
S139 src=cite kid=K002 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Real-number arithmetic: addition and multiplication are commutative and associative; multiplication distributes over addition; 0 is the additive identity and 1 is the multiplicative identity; every real number x has an additive inverse -x; every nonzero real number x has a multiplicative inverse 1/x.
S140 src=cite kid=K002 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Division by zero is undefined.
S141 src=cite kid=K003 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Ordering of real numbers: for every real x, exactly one of x > 0, x = 0, x < 0 is true; sums and products of nonnegative numbers are nonnegative; x squared is >= 0 for every real x.
S142 src=cite kid=K004 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Euclid's postulates: (1) a straight line segment can be drawn joining any two points; (2) any line segment can be extended indefinitely; (3) a circle can be drawn with any center and any radius; (4) all right angles are congruent; (5) parallel postulate: given a line and a point not on it, exactly one line through the point is parallel to the given line.
S143 src=cite kid=K005 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Rules of inference: modus ponens (from P and 'if P then Q', i.e.
S144 src=cite kid=K005 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: P=>Q, infer Q); proof by contradiction (if assuming 'not P' leads to a contradiction, infer P).
S145 src=cite kid=K101 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Divisibility: for integers a and b with a != 0, 'a divides b' (written a|b) holds if and only if (iff) there is an integer c with b = a * c.
S146 src=cite kid=K102 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Prime number: an integer p > 1 whose only positive divisors are 1 and p.
S147 src=cite kid=K103 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Composite number: an integer n > 1 that is not prime.
S148 src=cite kid=K104 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Congruence: for a positive integer n, 'a is congruent to b modulo n' (written a ≡ b (mod n)) holds if and only if (iff) n divides (a - b).
S149 src=cite kid=K105 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Rational number: a real number that can be written as p/q with integers p and q != 0.
S150 src=cite kid=K105 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Irrational number: a real number that is not rational.
S151 src=cite kid=K106 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Factorial: 0! = 1, and n! = n * (n-1)! for n >= 1.
S152 src=cite kid=K106 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Binomial coefficient: C(n,k) = n!/(k! * (n-k)!) for integers 0 <= k <= n.
S153 src=cite kid=K107 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Even and odd: an integer n is even if n = 2k for some integer k; n is odd if n = 2k + 1 for some integer k.
S154 src=cite kid=K108 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Triangle: three non-collinear points together with the segments joining them.
S155 src=cite kid=K108 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Interior angle: the angle inside the triangle at a vertex.
S156 src=cite kid=K108 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Median: the segment from a vertex to the midpoint of the opposite side.
S157 src=cite kid=K108 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Isosceles triangle: a triangle with (at least) two equal sides.
S158 src=cite kid=K108 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Right triangle: a triangle with one 90-degree angle.
S159 src=cite kid=K108 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Parallel lines: lines in a plane that never meet.
S160 src=cite kid=K109 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Perfect square: an integer of the form m^2 for some integer m.
S161 src=cite kid=K110 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Probability (finite, equally likely outcomes): the probability of an event is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the number of total outcomes.
S162 src=cite kid=K201 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Fundamental theorem of arithmetic: every integer greater than 1 is a product of prime numbers, uniquely up to order.
S163 src=cite kid=K202 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Euclid's lemma: if p is a prime number and p divides the product a * b, then p divides a or p divides b.
S164 src=cite kid=K203 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Bezout's identity: for integers a and b, there are integers x and y with a*x + b*y = gcd(a,b).
S165 src=cite kid=K204 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Pigeonhole principle: if more than n items are placed into n boxes, some box contains at least 2 items.
S166 src=cite kid=K205 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Pythagorean theorem: in a right triangle with legs a, b and hypotenuse c, a^2 + b^2 = c^2.
S167 src=cite kid=K206 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: There are infinitely many prime numbers.
S168 src=cite kid=K207 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Algebraic identities: (a+b)^2 = a^2+2ab+b^2; (a-b)^2 = a^2-2ab+b^2; a^2-b^2 = (a-b)(a+b), for all real numbers a and b.
S169 src=cite kid=K208 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Vertical angles are equal.
S170 src=cite kid=K208 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: If a transversal cuts two parallel lines, alternate interior angles are equal.
S171 src=cite kid=K209 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Triangle congruence criteria: SAS, ASA, SSS.
S172 src=cite kid=K209 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: (If two triangles satisfy any one of these criteria, all corresponding sides and angles are equal.)
S173 src=cite kid=K210 lic=-1 p=[-1,-1,-1] depth=1 live t=-1 r=0 taint=0: Midpoint theorem: the segment joining the midpoints of two sides of a triangle is parallel to the third side and half its length.
